tegral as a repeated integral:      \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}}[{\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{4}}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}}[{\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{4}}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}}{y}^{2}[{\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{4}}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}}{y}^{2}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}}{y}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡{e}^{4}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡{e}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}}{y}^{2}\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}}2{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}}2{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\frac{2}{3}[{y}^{3}]_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}((\\sqrt[3]{6})^{3}-{0}^{3}) \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-73591/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d237f9fb-b5d2-53e0-bc28-ee50d9e08852"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73591"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-72175/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "30bd559f-9d08-5288-ad54-c9ae60b7a556" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72175/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "00abc4c9-f9b1-575b-8794-8874828aecc1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72175/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "5e409c45-1ccd-5923-a127-7664c2de19e2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72175/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "6400e3ab-6c70-5278-bfca-a0962f17e481" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72175/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "179dede6-5b04-58bf-a1e7-21b80fd01fdd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72175/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "034ae56c-bed7-531e-8adb-eb0c1a952cec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-72175/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer-field/choices ["q-72175/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-72175/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-72175/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-72175/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-72175/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-72175" :question/id #uuid "80bfbd6a-391f-520f-a0ad-dc736395685b" :question/math-academy-id "q-72175" :question/problem "Which of the following equalities are true given that\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{2},\\,-\\sqrt{3}\\le y\\le 2}.$\n\n- ${∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{2}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$\n- ${∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y$\n- ${∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$" :question/worked-solution "We notice that:  \n\n- the limits for the variable $x$ are from $0$ to $\\sqrt{2}$, and\n\n- the limits for the variable $y$ are from $-\\sqrt{3}$ to $2.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the region of integration is rectangular, we can simply swap the order of integration. This gives\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}[{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{2}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-72175/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8f012d0-444a-5035-8a72-a053de312d63"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72175"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129645/selection/d1b4719a847d592cdee696261ea1e131561c6b187c4084947cffc06e6100096c" :answer/id #uuid "e8fb6df7-a4fa-5012-a1ad-833472d48fa0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-2e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129645/selection/087d6195df78ac19ad68ba3746305a749712648815fc499a6add393278e08471" :answer/id #uuid "eb505034-f07c-5969-8499-ba1888c68370" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129645/selection/ace37c2040207cebb14b55c05840a4c383db24d63f2349cf49f8db6a85f5faeb" :answer/id #uuid "543cbf94-8e83-5ec0-907f-853cffec26f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129645/selection/5a1fe28b022029f27455dc36a9cc0dbfd0eced1186649091706824f56db6ba8d" :answer/id #uuid "54d1cd5a-0eb6-58c9-a9be-42ccd1b1e77e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129645/selection/2a28a53216361474017108aa9cf0fffd0fb392524d53aeb00b78355e4fa703c6" :answer/id #uuid "7b85eead-6ea4-5ffa-9dbf-05336f91eea9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129645/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6e57e113-8971-5956-b522-f72888d2a0ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129645/selection/087d6195df78ac19ad68ba3746305a749712648815fc499a6add393278e08471" :answer-field/choices ["q-129645/selection/d1b4719a847d592cdee696261ea1e131561c6b187c4084947cffc06e6100096c" "q-129645/selection/087d6195df78ac19ad68ba3746305a749712648815fc499a6add393278e08471" "q-129645/selection/ace37c2040207cebb14b55c05840a4c383db24d63f2349cf49f8db6a85f5faeb" "q-129645/selection/5a1fe28b022029f27455dc36a9cc0dbfd0eced1186649091706824f56db6ba8d" "q-129645/selection/2a28a53216361474017108aa9cf0fffd0fb392524d53aeb00b78355e4fa703c6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129645" :question/id #uuid "19c5efcf-01ef-5fbf-9f64-6c90653aec20" :question/math-academy-id "q-129645" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant. \n\nMaking a substitution $xy=u,$ $\\text{d}y=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}u,$ we get.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}x{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x[{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x[{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{x}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{e}^{u}]_{0}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{x}-1)\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{x}-1)\\,\\text{d}x & =[{e}^{x}-x]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(e-1)-(1-0) \\\\  & =e-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-129645/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8f012d0-444a-5035-8a72-a053de312d63"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129645"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-72130/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "ad446f99-b842-5a1f-9781-495a0a9d2b67" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72130/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "5e90189e-2806-57a2-b52a-fd24ed9e16d1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72130/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "7422fa66-43e0-55d7-9168-7e88966ee1c9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72130/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "072bd4be-d5ca-508b-bb03-7d6816e97526" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72130/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "597056b1-7272-5392-a083-d7781bb54a94" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72130/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1cd3d376-0519-52d1-9277-4a01bb672fba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-72130/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-72130/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-72130/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-72130/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-72130/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-72130/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-72130" :question/id #uuid "81aee10d-0b2a-5edf-957e-80f23e4fc897" :question/math-academy-id "q-72130" :question/problem "Which of the following equalities are true given that\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\le y\\le 1}.$\n\n- ${∬}_{D}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y$\n- ${∬}_{D}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$\n- ${∬}_{D}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\text{d}A={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$" :question/worked-solution "We notice that:\n\n- the limits for the variable $x$ are from $1$ to $2$, and\n\n- the limits for the variable $y$ are from $\\frac{1}{2}$ to $1.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the region of integration is rectangular, we can simply swap the order of integration. This gives\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-72130/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8f012d0-444a-5035-8a72-a053de312d63"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72130"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129644/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "7fdd52f9-d9bb-561c-82cc-7d3ff4953215" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129644/selection/5521c093c4d60c23d630a99bc791ac7318f4615e164361df756510ffc0408a97" :answer/id #uuid "47b59bc1-a2e3-51ff-a5f0-e8840e10e3b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129644/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "edd04d7b-dedb-5fda-bed9-bdc414835e4a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129644/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "478dad29-8876-5cf2-8e53-eae1efe9d64b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129644/selection/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" :answer/id #uuid "2a17e6de-212c-5c19-a087-c7127d5dd99c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129644/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "40157fc0-c0fc-5196-8030-be76f4c42d5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129644/selection/5521c093c4d60c23d630a99bc791ac7318f4615e164361df756510ffc0408a97" :answer-field/choices ["q-129644/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-129644/selection/5521c093c4d60c23d630a99bc791ac7318f4615e164361df756510ffc0408a97" "q-129644/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-129644/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-129644/selection/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129644" :question/id #uuid "a687ad08-b4b5-5aee-9377-c64aedd03364" :question/math-academy-id "q-129644" :question/problem "${\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(x+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}(x+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\,{[xy+\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}[(2x+\\frac{8}{3})-(x+\\frac{1}{3})]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(x+\\frac{7}{3})\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(x+\\frac{7}{3})\\,\\text{d}x & ={[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{7x}{3}]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{7}{3})-(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{7}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-129644/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8f012d0-444a-5035-8a72-a053de312d63"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129644"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73601/selection/6af0fcb15cec073875595b67cefcb2d554a7787b4f5efaf9c8a1e6675ea8c9a1" :answer/id #uuid "c84cf251-b895-5499-9ab1-deaba449235c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73601/selection/4c409a7f686a96b1e9e2fe51ac0d388e249cceb1b578f8428a17a028897baaf0" :answer/id #uuid "c794778d-d6a8-5ca4-b34b-99a57dec5677" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73601/selection/93bfa2b0c9c76f21bc3639bb8b61f5185486333bfd62e5ac2bb408813fa45f9a" :answer/id #uuid "4a7c1d00-a2ef-5bea-b85a-0a5d489f8b3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73601/selection/6b96074fa3d182fe8e2e2b5f0adf96fee3abafe1e8b87f02c5951e275fa84778" :answer/id #uuid "46d53d8e-95e7-59b1-81ca-034ea68d39d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73601/selection/f3dac89f2ee5e33877fb0ae412fdefdc0cdcceb7dcdcd6e702e1e3ff0391e011" :answer/id #uuid "956aba47-a7f4-5829-9b40-c75f7f783f92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73601/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "42b4ebdd-4a5c-579a-8412-a14370d6b40a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73601/selection/4c409a7f686a96b1e9e2fe51ac0d388e249cceb1b578f8428a17a028897baaf0" :answer-field/choices ["q-73601/selection/6af0fcb15cec073875595b67cefcb2d554a7787b4f5efaf9c8a1e6675ea8c9a1" "q-73601/selection/4c409a7f686a96b1e9e2fe51ac0d388e249cceb1b578f8428a17a028897baaf0" "q-73601/selection/93bfa2b0c9c76f21bc3639bb8b61f5185486333bfd62e5ac2bb408813fa45f9a" "q-73601/selection/6b96074fa3d182fe8e2e2b5f0adf96fee3abafe1e8b87f02c5951e275fa84778" "q-73601/selection/f3dac89f2ee5e33877fb0ae412fdefdc0cdcceb7dcdcd6e702e1e3ff0391e011"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73601" :question/id #uuid "f11f8b7c-36a0-5fac-8519-f4d43bfce23c" :question/math-academy-id "q-73601" :question/problem "Evaluate the repeated integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{e}^{-1}}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{{3}^{x}}{y}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{{e}^{-1}}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{{3}^{x}}{y}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{3}^{x}[{\\int }_{{e}^{-1}}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{3}^{x}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡y]_{{e}^{-1}}^{{e}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{3}^{x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡{e}^{3}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡{e}^{-1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{3}^{x}(3+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4\\cdot {3}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}4\\cdot {3}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =4{[\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =4(\\frac{{3}^{1}-{3}^{0}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73601/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8f012d0-444a-5035-8a72-a053de312d63"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73601"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6097"] :question/problem "Evaluate the repeated integral $\\displaystyle \\int_{2}^{4}  \\int_{0}^{2} \\dfrac{x^3}{y^2} \\, \\textrm{d}x  \\, \\textrm{d}y.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{4}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}(\\frac{{2}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{{0}^{4}}{4})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{4}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =4{[-\\frac{1}{y}]}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =4(-\\frac{1}{4}-(-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6098"] :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle \\iint \\limits_{D} \\dfrac y{x^2} \\, \\textrm d A$, where \n$D=\\left\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\:2 \\leq x \\leq 4,\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 3\\right\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[-\\frac{y}{x}]}_{2}^{4}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(-\\frac{y}{4}-(-\\frac{y}{2}))\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{y}{4}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{y}{4}\\,\\text{d}y & ={[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6099"] :question/problem "Which of the following equalities are true given that\n$D = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 2, \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1 \\big\\}.$\n\n- $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}} \\,\\text{d}A  = \\int_{0}^{1}  \\int_{0}^{2}e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,  \\text{d}y \\, \\text{d}x$\n\n- $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\text{d}A  = \\int_{0}^{2}  \\int_{0}^{1} e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\, \\text{d}y\\,  \\text{d}x$\n\n- $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}} \\,\\text{d}A = \\int_{0}^{1}  \\int_{0}^{2}e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,  \\text{d}x \\, \\text{d}y$" :question/worked-solution "We notice that: \n\n- the limits for the variable $x$ are from ${\\color{blue}0}$ to ${\\color{blue}2}$, and\n\n- the limits for the variable $y$ are from ${\\color{red}0}$ to ${\\color{red}1}.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the region of integration is rectangular, we can simply swap the order of integration. This gives\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}} \\,\\text{d}A  \n= \\int_{\\color{blue}0}^{\\color{blue}{2}} \\left[ \\int_{\\color{red}0}^{\\color{red}1} e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\text{d}{\\color{red}y} \\right] \\text{d}{\\color{blue}x} .\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"." :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
